      "pins": ["J6.3", "J11.3", "R9.1", "R9.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(J6-Pin_3)", "Net-(J11-Pin_3)"],
      "observed": "R9 is a 0 Ω resistor connecting J6 pin 3 directly to J11 pin 3. Both are servo signal pins, so the two channels are electrically tied together.",
      "expected": "In PWM mode the two servo headers should have independent signal lines; the specification says each gets its own GPIO line and that the serial-mode bridge is made with R13/R14.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R9\") (value \"0\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J6\") (pin \"3\") ...)(node (ref \"R9\") (pin \"1\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J11\") (pin \"3\") ...)(node (ref \"R9\") (pin \"2\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "each servo header's signal pin gets its own independent 1 kΩ-buffered GPIO line"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The two servo signal channels cannot operate independently in PWM mode; their outputs are coupled and may interfere with one another.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows the two servo signal pins connected through 0 Ω R9, contradicting the specified independent PWM channels. The specification instead assigns the serial-mode signal bridge to R13/R14."
}

